ai_response:
Based on the retrieved context, under Section 4(1)(b) of the RTI Act, the Department of Administrative Reforms and Public Grievances (DARPG) is required to publish the following organisational functions, budget allocations, and subsidy programmes proactively on its website:

* Organisational structure, including names and designations of all officials;
* Information about its budget allocations and expenditures;
* Details of subsidy programmes implemented by the department.

This information is mandatorily required to be published on the website as a statutory disclosure under Section 4(1)(b) of the RTI Act.

Source: The Right to Information Act, 2005 (Section 4(1)(b))
